I come home.
Nina is at the door.
She says: "Hello, Maya."
I say: "Hello, Nina."
"I have a Danish phone number now," I say.
"My number is twelve, thirty-four, fifty-six, seventy-eight."
Nina writes the number.
"Good," she says.
"My number is eighty-seven, sixty-five, forty-three, twenty-one."
I write the number.
"Thank you, Nina," I say.
Now I have her number.
And she has my number.
We are neighbours and friends.
